1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,395
When Bookings and Calendars are both on, every booking is also an event

2
00:00:05,395 --> 00:00:10,189
on a shared calendar, and a calendar can close the dates of a booking product.

3
00:00:10,189 --> 00:00:14,641
This video shows the Bookings calendar, how to add older bookings to the

4
00:00:14,641 --> 00:00:17,780
calendar, and how to block dates with a calendar.

5
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:27,315
Bookings sells dates, nights and times, and the Bookings page keeps a calendar

6
00:00:27,315 --> 00:00:28,725
of what is booked.

7
00:00:28,725 --> 00:00:33,425
With the Calendars feature on, the same bookings also appear on the shared

8
00:00:33,425 --> 00:00:36,774
calendar, next to the rest of your team's schedule.

9
00:00:36,774 --> 00:00:39,300
There is no extra feature to turn on.

10
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:42,938
One calendar called Bookings holds them all.

11
00:00:42,938 --> 00:00:47,038
Each event is named after the product and the buyer, and lasts as

12
00:00:47,038 --> 00:00:48,539
long as the booking.

13
00:00:48,539 --> 00:00:53,102
It is tentative while the booking is held or requested, confirmed once it

14
00:00:53,102 --> 00:00:57,260
is booked, and cancelled when the booking is cancelled or expires.

15
00:01:01,463 --> 00:01:03,925
Open Commerce, Bookings, Calendar.

16
00:01:03,925 --> 00:01:09,772
It shows each month's dates and times, with the places taken out of the places available.

17
00:01:09,772 --> 00:01:12,603
Use the arrows to move to another month.

18
00:01:13,054 --> 00:01:17,313
Choose Open in calendar to see the same bookings on the shared calendar,

19
00:01:17,313 --> 00:01:20,754
where they sit next to everything else on your calendars.

20
00:01:21,207 --> 00:01:22,948
Open a booking's event.

21
00:01:22,948 --> 00:01:26,011
It shows the product, the buyer and the time.

22
00:01:26,011 --> 00:01:30,395
It can only be changed from the booking itself, so the calendar and

23
00:01:30,395 --> 00:01:32,197
the orders always agree.

24
00:01:32,647 --> 00:01:37,055
Back on the Bookings calendar, Sync to calendar adds the events of every

25
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:39,767
booking from today on, held ones included.

26
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:44,231
It is meant for bookings made before Calendars was turned on, and running

27
00:01:44,231 --> 00:01:46,547
it again changes only what differs.

28
00:01:50,749 --> 00:01:54,424
A calendar can also close the dates of a booking product.

29
00:01:54,424 --> 00:01:58,624
Edit a product, such as the Alpine Lakes Tour, and find Block with

30
00:01:58,624 --> 00:02:00,899
calendar in its booking settings.

31
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:05,581
Choose a calendar, and anything busy on it closes the times of this

32
00:02:05,581 --> 00:02:09,290
product, and the dates or nights when it is busy that day.

33
00:02:09,290 --> 00:02:13,173
Use it to keep one guide or one vehicle from being sold twice

34
00:02:13,173 --> 00:02:18,100
across products, or to close dates that a team calendar marks as out of office.

35
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:26,438
Your team sees what is booked in one place, next to meetings, time

36
00:02:26,438 --> 00:02:30,290
off and the rest of the schedule, without opening each order.

37
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:34,169
A held or requested booking shows as tentative.

38
00:02:34,169 --> 00:02:38,833
Once it is booked its event is confirmed, and a cancelled booking's event

39
00:02:38,833 --> 00:02:42,080
is cancelled, so the calendar shows what is real.

40
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:45,733
The Bookings calendar is private at first.

41
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:50,753
Share it with your staff under Calendars, Manage Calendars, so guides and the

42
00:02:50,753 --> 00:02:52,930
front desk see the same dates.

43
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:57,579
And when a guide, a room or a vehicle is shared by several

44
00:02:57,579 --> 00:03:02,270
products, Block with calendar keeps the same day from being sold twice.

45
00:03:04,270 --> 00:03:09,256
Every booking shows on the calendar, and a calendar can close what Bookings sells.

46
00:03:09,256 --> 00:03:10,730
Thanks for watching.

